1
00:00:07,198 --> 00:00:09,517
Whiskers and the Yellow Tram.

2
00:00:19,129 --> 00:00:22,747
One summer morning, a wonderful smell floated in.

3
00:00:22,947 --> 00:00:25,804
Grilled sardines? I must be dreaming.

4
00:00:26,004 --> 00:00:28,804
You're not dreaming! Look, a dog on a yellow scooter!

5
00:00:33,433 --> 00:00:36,488
Good morning, little cats! I'm Tiago. Would you like a sardine?

6
00:00:36,688 --> 00:00:38,280
Would I LIKE a sardine!

7
00:00:42,356 --> 00:00:46,606
I'm riding home to Lisbon. Tonight the whole city grills sardines and dances!

8
00:00:46,806 --> 00:00:49,022
Sardines and dancing? Can we come?

9
00:00:49,222 --> 00:00:51,065
Of course! Hop in the sidecar!

10
00:00:51,265 --> 00:00:53,533
I'll guard the house! Bring me back a story!

11
00:00:59,270 --> 00:01:02,444
So off they puttered, all day and all night.

12
00:01:17,593 --> 00:01:20,627
Wake up, friends! There it is. Lisbon, and the river Tagus!

13
00:01:29,132 --> 00:01:30,714
What an enormous red bridge!

14
00:01:33,683 --> 00:01:38,627
By the river stood the Tower of Belém, where explorers once sailed out to sea.

15
00:01:43,810 --> 00:01:46,524
And here they bake the best custard tarts in the world!

16
00:01:46,724 --> 00:01:49,658
One for me, and one for me, and one for me...

17
00:02:01,485 --> 00:02:04,990
I sneezed on purpose. Cinnamon is good for fur.

18
00:02:05,190 --> 00:02:07,443
Ha! Now I must go and help my grandma.

19
00:02:07,643 --> 00:02:12,682
Take tram twenty-eight to the castle. Meet me at sunset at Avó's house, the one with blue tiles!

20
00:02:12,882 --> 00:02:15,883
Tram twenty-eight. Blue tiles. Come on, Whiskers!

21
00:02:18,852 --> 00:02:22,916
The little yellow tram rattled up the steep, narrow hills.

22
00:02:31,421 --> 00:02:34,395
Laundry lines! Painted tiles! Whiskers, look!

23
00:02:34,595 --> 00:02:37,988
Mm-hm. I'm watching. With my eyes closed.

24
00:02:43,725 --> 00:02:45,524
Our stop, Whiskers! Come on!

25
00:02:50,707 --> 00:02:52,842
Whiskers? Whiskers! Wait for me!

26
00:02:58,025 --> 00:03:01,948
Luna searched the whole castle, but Whiskers was nowhere.

27
00:03:07,131 --> 00:03:11,303
Dom Pavão, keeper of the castle. Why so sad, little cat?

28
00:03:11,503 --> 00:03:15,341
I lost my friend. He's orange, and round, and loves sardines.

29
00:03:15,541 --> 00:03:18,623
Come! From my wall you can see all of Lisbon.

30
00:03:26,021 --> 00:03:29,062
So many roofs. So many streets. I miss him already.

31
00:03:32,031 --> 00:03:34,926
Far away, Whiskers woke up all alone.

32
00:03:35,126 --> 00:03:37,516
Luna? Luna! Oh no. Where am I?

33
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:48,718
Up a hill, down a hill. And every street smells of sardines!

34
00:03:56,669 --> 00:03:58,944
There's the castle! I'm coming, Luna!

35
00:04:05,788 --> 00:04:08,947
You must be Whiskers! Tiago told me. Have a sardine, dear.

36
00:04:12,469 --> 00:04:17,013
Thank you. But I can't. Sardines don't taste right without Luna.

37
00:04:17,213 --> 00:04:20,294
We have a word for that. Saudade. Missing someone you love.

38
00:04:20,494 --> 00:04:23,497
So let's play a fado, loud enough to reach the castle!

39
00:04:35,878 --> 00:04:39,361
Avó Lurdes' fado! Follow the music, Luna!

40
00:04:45,098 --> 00:04:45,941
Whiskers!

41
00:04:46,141 --> 00:04:47,014
Luna!

42
00:04:53,858 --> 00:04:57,587
That night, under a thousand lanterns, Lisbon danced.

43
00:05:05,538 --> 00:05:09,233
Now they taste perfect. One for you, and one for me.

44
00:05:13,309 --> 00:05:15,961
I had saudade too, Whiskers. All afternoon.

45
00:05:16,161 --> 00:05:20,176
Next time I fall asleep on a tram... please wake me up.

46
00:05:31,449 --> 00:05:34,957
Tiago drove them home, with a present from Avó.

47
00:05:35,157 --> 00:05:37,042
You're back! Did you bring me a story?

48
00:05:37,242 --> 00:05:40,658
A story, and a sardine. And Pip? I missed you.

49
00:05:40,858 --> 00:05:46,495
Because missing someone means they live in your heart. In Lisbon, they call it saudade.

